  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The vectors a and b are given: a has components 3 and −2, and b has components −1 and 4. (a) Calculate 2a − b. (b) Calculate a + b. (c) Hence determine |3a|."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Vector arithmetic works one row at a time — top with top, bottom with bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p180_q05.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p180-q05 from workbook page 180."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Double a.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 × (3, −2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2a = (6, −4)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Subtract b component by component.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "6 − (−1) = 7 and −4 − 4 = −8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2a − b = (7, −8)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Add a and b.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "3 + (−1) = 2 and −2 + 4 = 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: a + b = (2, 2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Find |a|.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "|a|² = 3² + (−2)² = 9 + 4 = 13"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: |a| = √13"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 5,
      "instruction": "Scale the magnitude.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "|3a| = 3|a| = 3√13"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: |3a| = 3√13 ≈ 10.8"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Scale and combine components separately for parts a and b, then use |3a| = 3|a| with Pythagoras for part c."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) 2a − b = (7, −8)  (b) a + b = (2, 2)  (c) |3a| = 3√13 ≈ 10.8"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Each component of a column vector describes movement in a direction independent of the other, so operations act on them separately — there is no mixing between rows. Multiplying a vector by 3 triples both components, which triples the hypotenuse too, so |3a| = 3|a|; computing 3a = (9, −6) and starting Pythagoras again gives the same √117 = 3√13."
    }
  ],
